<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip (Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-5> ;
    schema:about "Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Reproduction of the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table or bifurcation figures; 3D somite epithelialization mechanics; a derivation of the FGF8-bead / SU5402 / electroporation somite-size shifts from the switch dynamics (they remain constants in the lab-frame simulator and the reference JSON)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D cell-based strip with explicit progenitor division and mRNA partitioning: exported level 0.994 vs closed form 1.000, gradient length 370.5 vs 360.7 um, front 698.8 +/- 7.0 um vs lambda_m ln(m_exit/m_crit) = 694.4 um, S_2D = 148.2 um, dilution shift 276-286 um vs closed form 271 um",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Characteristic-upwind 1D advection-decay PDE solver dm/dt + v_g dm/dx = -k_d m (L2 relative error 0.0009 vs analytical exponential)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Goldbeter-type 3-variable RA/FGF8/Cyp26 switch coupled to the mRNA gradient: saddle-nodes m_SN_lo = 0.184 / m_SN_hi = 0.546, hysteretic cell-trajectory front x_sw = 720.4 um, transition width 198 um vs 792 um, reverse switch at m = 0.675",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Lab-frame FGF8 wavefront-gated somite boundary simulator across wild-type, ectopic FGF8 bead (S_ant = 97.5 um, S_post = 202.5 um), SU5402 (S = 215.0 um) and k_d = 0 ablation control (N = 0 somites) - with the perturbation shifts entered as constants, not derived",
        "reported_in_source: Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422 cell-autonomous fgf8 mRNA decay gradient m(x) = m_0 exp(-k_d x / v_g) generated by tailbud-restricted transcription and axis elongation",
        "reported_in_source: Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232 determination front threshold positioning x* = (v_g/k_d) ln(m_0/m_crit) and ectopic FGF8 bead / SU5402 somite size perturbations",
        "reported_in_source: Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 bistability of the RA -| FGF -> Cyp26 -| RA double-negative loop defining a sharp determination threshold",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows of a Wikimedia specimen whose species is labelled avian/vertebrate, not confirmed as Gallus gallus",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D strip: PSM cells do not divide, all elongation comes from progenitor division (no Benazeraf 2010 motility gradient), rows are coupled only through FGF8 smoothing (no mechanics)",
        "transfer_boundary: Goldbeter switch functional forms follow the 2007 paper but the dimensionless parameter values (K_A = 0.18, K_I = 0.6, k_C = 2, n = 4, tau_sw = 10 min) are this script's bistable-regime choice; the switch is evaluated along a 1D cell trajectory and is NOT embedded in the 2D strip" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21193>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2006.01.018>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02332>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09151> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Advection-Reaction mRNA Decay Wavefront & Threshold Phase-Gating (Somitogenesis)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.62e-01 .

