    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py; output: docs/media/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: c932f4a1dd2d2a7154d419f019c4a647891c78e7cc462bb8f1d3ef6cb210100e; artifact_sha256: 61b31ffd1e1b1344790d330a58240354a24d2ec245281da77adea61593631ff4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json=0a4d2aabb27a874d..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/scout_manifest.json=a38a686592f1ffd0...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422 cell-autonomous fgf8 mRNA decay gradient m(x) = m_0 exp(-k_d x / v_g) generated by tailbud-restricted transcription and axis elongation | Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232 determination front threshold positioning x* = (v_g/k_d) ln(m_0/m_crit) and ectopic FGF8 bead / SU5402 somite size perturbations | Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 bistability of the RA -| FGF -> Cyp26 -| RA double-negative loop defining a sharp determination threshold; reconstructed_in_script: Characteristic-upwind 1D advection-decay PDE solver dm/dt + v_g dm/dx = -k_d m (L2 relative error 0.0009 vs analytical exponential) | Lab-frame FGF8 wavefront-gated somite boundary simulator across wild-type, ectopic FGF8 bead (S_ant = 97.5 um, S_post = 202.5 um), SU5402 (S = 215.0 um) and k_d = 0 ablation control (N = 0 somites) - with the perturbation shifts entered as constants, not derived | Goldbeter-type 3-variable RA/FGF8/Cyp26 switch coupled to the mRNA gradient: saddle-nodes m_SN_lo = 0.184 / m_SN_hi = 0.546, hysteretic cell-trajectory front x_sw = 720.4 um, transition width 198 um vs 792 um, reverse switch at m = 0.675 | 2D cell-based strip with explicit progenitor division and mRNA partitioning: exported level 0.994 vs closed form 1.000, gradient length 370.5 vs 360.7 um, front 698.8 +/- 7.0 um vs lambda_m ln(m_exit/m_crit) = 694.4 um, S_2D = 148.2 um, dilution shift 276-286 um vs closed form 271 um | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows of a Wikimedia specimen whose species is labelled avian/vertebrate, not confirmed as Gallus gallus | Goldbeter switch functional forms follow the 2007 paper but the dimensionless parameter values (K_A = 0.18, K_I = 0.6, k_C = 2, n = 4, tau_sw = 10 min) are this script's bistable-regime choice; the switch is evaluated along a 1D cell trajectory and is NOT embedded in the 2D strip | 2D strip: PSM cells do not divide, all elongation comes from progenitor division (no Benazeraf 2010 motility gradient), rows are coupled only through FGF8 smoothing (no mechanics); does_not_claim: Reproduction of the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table or bifurcation figures; 3D somite epithelialization mechanics; a derivation of the FGF8-bead / SU5402 / electroporation somite-size shifts from the switch dynamics (they remain constants in the lab-frame simulator and the reference JSON)]" ;
