    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every modelling function carries a Law number, the cited paper and the Lean theorem name in its docstring (Laws 1-5 in the module docstring L23-L94; function docstrings at L154, L170, L220, L238, L318, L338, L378, L433, L621, L654, L873), and `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.yaml` registers 5 equations with lean_locus and code_locus pointing at the current line ranges (L33-L162). Deductions: the Goldbeter equation numbering is asserted, not verified (-4); the hard-coded 67.5 um electroporation shift (L271-L274) and the 52.5/65 um cycle shifts (L566-L584) cite no equation or figure (-4); Panel H's somite-boundary rendering and the 0.7-row mediolateral smoothing are design choices without a cited basis (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py L271–L274: Electroporation delta_x = 67.5 um hard-coded with a comment but no equation/figure citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py#L271-L274>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The core Dubrulle (2004) advection-decay PDE and the (2001) threshold law are implemented as published (L154-L235, L2 error 0.0009). Pass 3 adds the Goldbeter (2007) double-negative loop with the paper's functional forms (Hill repression of Fgf8 by RA, Hill induction of Cyp26 by FGF, Michaelis-Menten Cyp26-catalysed RA degradation; L318-L336) and shows genuine bistability (3 roots for m in [0.184, 0.546], monostable high-FGF posteriorly and low-FGF anteriorly, L338-L431), hysteresis along a cell trajectory and the one-division-equals-one-half-life dilution law realised in an explicit cell-based strip (L654-L870). Deductions: the lab-frame somite-train simulator still enters the bead (-52.5/+52.5 um), SU5402 (+65 um) and electroporation (67.5 um) shifts as constants instead of deriving them from a perturbed gradient or the new switch (L566-L584, L271-L274) (-6); the switch parameters are this script's choice, not the 2007 table, and the dynamic front lags the saddle-node by 110 um (slow passage at tau_sw = 10 min) so x_sw = 720 um is tuned-adjacent rather than predicted (-4); the switch is evaluated along one trajectory and not embedded in the 2D strip, whose determination is still the graded threshold on a smoothed field (-3); the strip's progenitor pool has no PSM division and makes all elongation proliferative (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py L566–L584: Bead/SU5402 somite shifts hard-coded per cycle (s_c = S0 - 52.5 etc.), not derived from the gradient or switch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py#L566-L584>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — Morphometric validation: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "measure_morphoeval() now returns 10 measurements, each with a reference_value, including the hysteretic front (720.4 vs 696.5 um), the bistable window (391.9 um), the 2D front (698.8 +/- 7.0 vs 694.4 um), the 2D somite length (148.2 vs 150 um) and the dilution shift (286 vs 271 um) (L983-L1120), with CV/SD/RMSE dispersion terms. Deductions: the 5-regime Pearson r = 0.9998 correlates `predicted_somite_length_um` read from the reference JSON with `observed_somite_length_um` read from the same JSON (L252-L291, L996-L999), so the headline validation is a table self-correlation, not a comparison of computed output with the paper (-7); two Pass 3 references are internal closed forms (window = lambda ln(m_SN_hi/m_SN_lo); front = lambda ln(m_exit/m_crit) with the simulated m_exit), i.e. consistency checks rather than literature values (-4); the 2D somite CV = 0.22 is 5x the observed chick 6.5/150 = 0.043 and the simulated dilution shifts exceed the closed form by 13-28 um systematically (first-determined-cell offset and smoothing bias), both disclosed in notes but not resolved (-4); no morphometric of the 2D strip is compared with the SEM specimen (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py L252–L291: evaluate_perturbation_regimes: S_pred_um is r['predicted_somite_length_um'] from the JSON; S_calc_um is computed but not used for r/RMSE <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py#L252-L291>",
        "datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json L82–L139: Regime table with observed_somite_length_um / observed_somite_sd_um lacking figure or table pinpoints <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json#L82-L139>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-2d-cell-based-psm-strip-mean-determination-front-x-2d-with-tailbud-division-dilution>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-2d-cell-based-strip-mean-somite-length-s-2d-cells-per-clock-cycle-x-cell-length>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-chick-psm-determination-front-distance-from-tailbud-x-v-g-k-d-ln-m-0-m-crit>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-chick-vertebrate-embryo-sem-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-dubrulle-et-al-2001-2004-5-regime-somite-length-prediction-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-ectopic-fgf8-bead-anterior-compressed-somite-length-s-ant>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-goldbeter-ra-fgf8-bistable-switch-hysteretic-determination-front-x-sw-cell-trajectory>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-ra-fgf8-bistable-hysteresis-window-width-along-the-psm-x-sn-lo-x-sn-hi>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-su5402-pharmacological-fgfr1-inhibition-enlarged-somite-length-s-su5402>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-measurement-tailbud-division-dilution-front-shift-delta-x-dil-no-division-control-minus-t-div-480-min-strip>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 closes both v2 remediation items with the closest honest reduced versions: a Goldbeter-type RA/FGF8/Cyp26 bistable switch coupled to the Dubrulle fgf8 mRNA gradient (Section 3b) that turns the graded threshold into a hysteretic front 4.0x sharper (198 vs 792 um) with a 392 um memory window, and a 2D cell-based PSM strip (Section 4b) with explicit tailbud progenitor division, binomial-like mRNA partitioning and per-row somite boundaries, whose exported level, gradient length, front position and dilution shift match the new closed forms (Law 5) to within cell-quantisation noise. Three Lean 4 theorems (6 total, 0 sorry) pin the loop sign, the hysteresis memory and the one-division-equals-one-half-life identity. The re-score is 86.2 (down from 90.9) because the deeper inspection exposed defects v2 had not deducted for: the lab-frame simulator hard-codes the bead/SU5402 shifts (L566-L584) and the 5-regime validation correlates JSON-stored predicted values with JSON-stored observed values whose figure pinpoints are unverified (L252-L291), the switch parameters are not the paper's, the switch is not embedded in the strip, and the strip's somite-length CV (0.22) is 5x the observed chick value. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.3, reproducibility 88.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 83, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_comparison.png: rendered output of 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py at d58a084, image/png, 1529122 B, 2352×2016 px, artifact_sha256 61b31ffd1e1b1344790d330a58240354a24d2ec245281da77adea61593631ff4 (sha256 61b31ffd1e1b1344790d330a58240354a24d2ec245281da77adea61593631ff4), spec_fingerprint c932f4a1dd2d2a7154d419f019c4a647891c78e7cc462bb8f1d3ef6cb210100e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c932f4a1dd2d2a7154d419f019c4a647891c78e7cc462bb8f1d3ef6cb210100e; artifact_sha256: 61b31ffd1e1b1344790d330a58240354a24d2ec245281da77adea61593631ff4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json=0a4d2aabb27a874d..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/scout_manifest.json=a38a686592f1ffd0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422 cell-autonomous fgf8 mRNA decay gradient m(x) = m_0 exp(-k_d x / v_g) generated by tailbud-restricted transcription and axis elongation | Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232 determination front threshold positioning x* = (v_g/k_d) ln(m_0/m_crit) and ectopic FGF8 bead / SU5402 somite size perturbations | Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 bistability of the RA -| FGF -> Cyp26 -| RA double-negative loop defining a sharp determination threshold; reconstructed_in_script: Characteristic-upwind 1D advection-decay PDE solver dm/dt + v_g dm/dx = -k_d m (L2 relative error 0.0009 vs analytical exponential) | Lab-frame FGF8 wavefront-gated somite boundary simulator across wild-type, ectopic FGF8 bead (S_ant = 97.5 um, S_post = 202.5 um), SU5402 (S = 215.0 um) and k_d = 0 ablation control (N = 0 somites) - with the perturbation shifts entered as constants, not derived | Goldbeter-type 3-variable RA/FGF8/Cyp26 switch coupled to the mRNA gradient: saddle-nodes m_SN_lo = 0.184 / m_SN_hi = 0.546, hysteretic cell-trajectory front x_sw = 720.4 um, transition width 198 um vs 792 um, reverse switch at m = 0.675 | 2D cell-based strip with explicit progenitor division and mRNA partitioning: exported level 0.994 vs closed form 1.000, gradient length 370.5 vs 360.7 um, front 698.8 +/- 7.0 um vs lambda_m ln(m_exit/m_crit) = 694.4 um, S_2D = 148.2 um, dilution shift 276-286 um vs closed form 271 um | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows of a Wikimedia specimen whose species is labelled avian/vertebrate, not confirmed as Gallus gallus | Goldbeter switch functional forms follow the 2007 paper but the dimensionless parameter values (K_A = 0.18, K_I = 0.6, k_C = 2, n = 4, tau_sw = 10 min) are this script's bistable-regime choice; the switch is evaluated along a 1D cell trajectory and is NOT embedded in the 2D strip | 2D strip: PSM cells do not divide, all elongation comes from progenitor division (no Benazeraf 2010 motility gradient), rows are coupled only through FGF8 smoothing (no mechanics); does_not_claim: Reproduction of the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table or bifurcation figures; 3D somite epithelialization mechanics; a derivation of the FGF8-bead / SU5402 / electroporation somite-size shifts from the switch dynamics (they remain constants in the lab-frame simulator and the reference JSON)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:1329-1357 vs 907-978 — Panel H (2D strip) is never compared with the SEM specimen. Add a boundary-straightness / somite-count / spacing-CV comparison between the strip and the segmented specimen rows, and confirm or re-label the specimen species.",
        "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:252-291 with datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/ fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json:82-139 — the 5-regime r = 0.9998 correlates JSON predicted values with JSON observed values whose Dubrulle (2001) figure/table pinpoints are unverified. Use S_calc_um (computed) for r/RMSE and add figure+panel pinpoints (or mark the observed values as reconstructed) for every regime.",
        "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:302-316 — GOLDBETER_SWITCH_PARAMS are this script's bistable-regime choice. Pin them to the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table, reproduce the paper's bistability diagram as a panel, and report x_sw as a prediction rather than a tuned-adjacent value (current slow-passage lag 110 um).",
        "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:566-584 and 271-274 — the lab-frame simulator enters the FGF8-bead (-52.5/+52.5 um), SU5402 (+65 um) and electroporation (67.5 um) front shifts as constants. Derive delta_x* from a Gaussian bead source added to m(x) and from a scaled K_A (SU5402) in the Section 3b switch, and feed the resulting per-cycle shifts into simulate_fgf8_somitogenesis.",
        "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:654-870 — embed the RA/FGF8 switch per cell in the 2D strip (currently a graded threshold on the smoothed field, L771-L779), add PSM cell division and a non-proliferative elongation term (Bénazéraf et al. 2010), and add mediolateral mechanical/community coupling so the somite-length CV (0.223) approaches the observed chick 0.043.",
        "remediation needed: 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py:873-900 and 1057-1067 — simulated dilution shifts exceed the closed form by 13-28 um at every T_div (first-determined-cell half-cell offset plus smoothing bias). Correct the front estimator (interpolate the F = m_crit crossing) or include the offset in the closed form, and state the residual in Panel I." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.62e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The (v_g, t_1/2) morphospace, the five experimental regimes and the k_d = 0 control are retained; Pass 3 adds a T_div sweep {240, 480, 960, 1920} min with a no-division ablation at fixed transcription whose simulated shifts (342, 286, 280, 278 um) decrease monotonically as the closed form predicts (329, 271, 252, 250 um) (L873-L900, Panel I inset), a per-cell switch constant --switch-ka, and CLI flags --t-div, --rows, --sigma-f, --print-pass3 that re-run the Pass 3 models (L1595-L1617). Deductions: K_A, sigma_F and n_rows are exposed but not swept or rendered, so their monotonic control is asserted not shown (-6); the dilution sweep's simulated shifts sit 13-28 um above the closed form at every T_div (systematic, see morphometric-validation) and the inset shows it without comment (-4); the bead strength and SU5402 dose remain non-parametric constants (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seeds (2003) for both the 1D simulator and the 2D strip with bitwise re-run checks in the self-test (L1497-L1500, L1548-L1550); --self-test extended to 6 blocks covering SHA-256, PDE error, conservation laws, specimen segmentation, switch bistability/monostability/hysteresis/steady-state residuals and strip closed forms (L1485-L1582), passing in ~2 s; default render 3.6 s; the GIF is byte-identical to Pass 2 (SHA-256 0da6319d...). Deductions: no requirements lock or recorded environment beyond the audit's checkpoint block (-4); when run under a read-only HOME matplotlib rebuilds its font cache in a temp dir and warns, which the invocation notes do not mention (-2); the PNG changed layout (2x3 -> 3x3) so Pass 2 artifact hashes no longer apply and no CSV of the measurements is emitted (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip — Source and data traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Four primary DOIs plus the newly cited Bénazéraf et al. (2010) are in the docstring, the dataset README and paper_citations.bib (L1-L22; datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/paper_citations.bib L1-L55); the specimen and scout manifest are SHA-256 pinned and verified at every run (L111-L142); the reference JSON now records the switch parameters with an explicit provenance flag (\"NOT the published parameter table\") and the 2D-strip reference outputs with the seed (JSON L141-L193). Deductions: the five \"observed\" somite lengths and SDs (98.0 +/- 8.0, 201.0 +/- 9.5, 214.0 +/- 10.0, 84.0 +/- 7.5 um) carry no figure/table/page pinpoint in Dubrulle et al. (2001) and could not be verified from the repository, so the validation's ground truth is traceable only to the JSON (-8); the reference JSON itself is not SHA-pinned (only hashed), so its edits are not fail-closed (-3); the Goldbeter equations are cited as \"Eqs. 1-3\" without verifying the paper's numbering (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
